description:
Currently, `send()` in `@supabase/supabase-js` v2.101.1 automatically falls back to REST API and logs a deprecation warning: 'Realtime send() is automatically falling back to REST API. This behavior will be deprecated in the future. Please use httpSend() explicitly for REST delivery.'

The replacement method `httpSend()` does not exist in v2.101.1. Once we upgrade to a version that ships `httpSend()`, switch these two locations:

**1. src/app/api/messages/route.ts:239**
```typescript
// OLD (current):
await supabase.channel(`chat:${conversationId}`).send({
  type: 'broadcast',
  event: 'new-message',
  payload: message,
});

// NEW (when httpSend is available):
await supabase.channel(`chat:${conversationId}`).httpSend({
  type: 'broadcast',
  event: 'new-message',
  payload: message,
});
```

**2. src/app/api/disputes/[id]/messages/route.ts:212**
```typescript
// OLD (current):
await supabase.channel(`dispute:${id}`).send({
  type: 'broadcast',
  event: 'new-mediation-message',
  payload: newMessage,
});

// NEW (when httpSend is available):
await supabase.channel(`dispute:${id}`).httpSend({
  type: 'broadcast',
  event: 'new-mediation-message',
  payload: newMessage,
});
```

**Why we're on the old method:** `httpSend()` is not available in the currently installed `@supabase/supabase-js@2.101.1`. The `send()` method works (just logs a warning). This will be resolved when the Supabase JS client is upgraded.

**Note:** `send()` in the current type definitions expects 2-3 arguments but works with a single object argument at runtime (type definition bug).
